    "result": "I implemented `shipping_cost` in `solution.py` and wrote 51 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes. The function uses exact `Fraction` arithmetic and rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` only at the end, so cases like 9.50 × 1.25 = 11.875 come out as 11.88. The billable weight is the larger of actual and volumetric weight, rounded up to the next 0.5 kg. The base charge, zone factor, free-shipping rule, and oversize surcharge follow the spec. Three of my first test expectations were wrong (a 121×10×10 box has a 2.42 kg volumetric weight, which bills at 2.5 kg); I corrected those tests to use thin boxes and left the implementation unchanged. The spec did not cover NaN or infinite inputs, so I chose to reject them with `ValueError`.",
